Sval: unregistering a JS process actor survives a process past its in-process actors

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2056174 (mozilla-central 7a8efbffdb7e, Firefox
154), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it.
JSActorService::UnregisterProcessActor appended InProcessChild::Singleton()
and InProcessParent::Singleton() to the managers it walks without checking
them, and both are null once XPCOM shutdown has torn the in-process actors
down, so unregistering a process actor then crashed on a null dereference.
DevTools unregisters its process actors when its last watcher goes.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 154.

diff --git a/dom/ipc/jsactor/JSActorService.cpp b/dom/ipc/jsactor/JSActorService.cpp
index bea1d44d9f..6068090bfd 100644
--- a/dom/ipc/jsactor/JSActorService.cpp
+++ b/dom/ipc/jsactor/JSActorService.cpp
@@ -321,8 +321,14 @@ void JSActorService::UnregisterProcessActor(const nsACString& aName) {
         }
         managers.AppendElement(cp);
       }
-      managers.AppendElement(InProcessChild::Singleton());
-      managers.AppendElement(InProcessParent::Singleton());
+      InProcessChild* ipChild = InProcessChild::Singleton();
+      if (ipChild) {
+        managers.AppendElement(ipChild);
+      }
+      InProcessParent* ipParent = InProcessParent::Singleton();
+      if (ipParent) {
+        managers.AppendElement(ipParent);
+      }
     } else {
       managers.AppendElement(ContentChild::GetSingleton());
     }
